                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game has A LOT of potential. I really really like the aesthetic and stylization of the characters, setting and props. \nCan't wait to see what outfits we can get for the characters!\n\nNow to the gameplay. It is very solid. The mechanics and rules are quite easy to understand. I think it would benefit from a playable tutorial, but right now the text tutorial explains itself pretty well. \nWhen you start a match from scratch as Villager the game runs well. Same with when you are the Monster and hosting the game, it runs well. The game becomes very buggy when either you join a match that has already started, or when the Host(Monster) leaves the game. \n\nUnfortunately, since the game doesn't have a big playerbase, finding matches as Villager is very difficult. But you CAN play against AI if you play as the Monster. And, other players can replace those bots if they join the match mid-way as Villager.\nI am recommending this game like its my religion from now on.\nI guess we can't really get much info if there's not enough players playing it.\nIt's kinda sad reading other people be mad at this game. I think it's cuz they expect a ready game from Steam, but they need to understand that this is a one-man made game and it is early access AND free. \nExpect it to be buggy. Try again another day. Don't quit on it just cuz your first try was uneventful. Please give the game a chance! Try playing both roles!",
